ticians on social media? Evidences from Brazilian state level elections |url=https://www.redalyc.org/journal/703/70373170005/html/ |journal=Revista Sociedade e Cultura |language=en |volume=25 |doi=10.5216/sec.v25.70812 |quote=(vii) Ideology (party): Despite that some international political science approaches consider party ideology a ‘démodé’ variable, Brazilian political scientists still vastly use it. Considering the objectives of our study, we classified the parties according to the literature concepts (ZUCCO JR., 2009), under which codes range from left (1) to right (5). Left: PSOL, PSTU, PCO, PCB. Center-left: PT, PCdoB, PDT. Center: PMDB, PSDB, PSB, PPS, PV. Center-right: PSD, PP, PR, PRB, PROS, PSC, PTB, PHS, SD. Right: DEM, PMN, PRP, PRTB, PSDC, PSL, PTdoB, PTC, PTN. |doi-access=free |archive-date=December 13, 2025 |access-date=August 8, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251213215231/https://www.redalyc.org/journal/703/70373170005/html/ |url-status=live }}
 }}|</ref>|
