e: Peter Hall |date=2019-05-16 |publisher=Bloomsbury Publishing |isbn=978-1-4725-8710-7 |language=en}}|{{Cite book |last=Bizeul |first=Yves |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=ScPkEAAAQBAJ&dq=%22neo+fascist%22%22svoboda%22&pg=PA253 |title=Rekonstruktion des Nationalmythos?: Frankreich, Deutschland und die Ukraine im Vergleich |date=2013-11-20 |publisher=V&R Unipress |isbn=978-3-8470-0181-2 |language=de}}|{{Cite journal |last=García Olascoaga |first=Omar |date=2018 |title=Presencia del neofascismo en las democracias europeas contemporáneas |url=https://dialnet.unirioja.es/servlet/articulo?codigo=6388199 |journal=REIS: Revista Española de Investigaciones Sociológicas |issue=162 |pages=3–20 |issn=0210-5233 |quote=Neo-fascism in Eastern Europe served as a primary force in Croatia with the Croatian Democratic Union (1990-2000); it has participated in government coalitions: the Greater Romania Party (1995), the Slovak National Party (1994-1998) and the Svoboda and Right Sector parties in the Ukraine (2014);}}|{{Cite web |last=Bandow |first=Doug |title=Europeans Watch Ukraine And Fear Russia: They Should Take Over NATO And Europe's Defense |url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/dougbandow/2014/03/10/europeans-watch-ukraine-and-fear-russia-they-should-take-over-nato-and-europes-defense/ |access-date=2025-02-04 |website=[[Forbes]] |language=en |quote=She apparently is in effective control of the new government, which includes cabinet ministers from the neo-fascist Svoboda Party.}}}}|</ref>|
