 | [[Social liberalism]]|ref|{{Cite book |last=Arrieta |first=Laura Ardila |url=https://www.google.com.ar/books/edition/La_costa_nostra/6stl0AEACAAJ?hl=es |title=La costa nostra |date=2023 |publisher=Rey Naranjo Editores |isbn=978-628-7589-17-9 |language=es |quote=Esa impresión encontraría aún más argumentos algunos años después, en 1992, cuando el exmandatario arrancaba el camino como senador con su movimiento liberal Voluntad Popular y, ya sin armas, esa guerrilla hacía la transición al partido político Alianza Democrática M-19 (AD M-19). |trans-quote=That impression would find even more support a few years later, in 1992, when the former president began his career as a senator with his liberal movement Popular Will and, now without weapons, that guerrilla group was transitioning to the political party Democratic Alliance M-19 (AD M-19).}}|</ref>|
 | [[Social democracy]]|ref| name="FP"|{{cite web |title=Recognizing Juan Guaidó as Venezuela's Leader Isn't a Coup. It's an Embrace of Democracy. |url=https://foreignpolicy.com/2019/02/06/recognizing-juan-guaido-as-venezuelas-leader-isnt-a-coup-its-an-embrace-of-democracy-nicolas-maduro-sanctions-icc/ |website=Foreign Policy |date=February 2024}}|</ref>|}}

